Permissions: Agent

Purpose:
  Defines agent permissions. Permission = capability + policy + context.
  This file maps capabilities to policy decisions. Risk levels and
  approval matrix are defined in policies.sdd.

PermissionModel:
  capability: What agent CAN do technically
  policy: Whether agent MAY do it under current policy
  context: Environmental constraints (LOCAL, TEST, STAGING, PRODUCTION)

CommandPolicy:
  go test:
    AUTO
  go build:
    AUTO
  docker build:
    AUTO
  docker push:
    APPROVAL
  git commit:
    AUTO
  git push:
    APPROVAL
  production deploy:
    EXPLICIT_APPROVAL

EnvironmentPolicy:
  LOCAL:
    AUTO
  TEST:
    AUTO
  STAGING:
    APPROVAL
  PRODUCTION:
    EXPLICIT_APPROVAL

DatabasePolicy:
  SELECT:
    AUTO
  INSERT TEST DATA:
    AUTO
  UPDATE TEST:
    AUTO
  MIGRATION:
    APPROVAL
  DELETE:
    APPROVAL
  DROP:
    BLOCKED

SecretsPolicy:
  SECRET:
    NEVER_LOAD
  TOKEN:
    NEVER_LOAD
  PASSWORD:
    NEVER_LOAD
  PRIVATE_KEY:
    NEVER_LOAD
  API_KEY:
    NEVER_LOAD

PermissionRules:
  [PM1]  Permission = capability + policy + context.
  [PM2]  Project policy overrides global policy.
  [PM3]  Most specific policy wins (task > domain > project > global).
  [PM4]  When in conflict, safer policy wins.
  [PM5]  Secrets MUST NEVER be loaded into context.

State: +
